# Trivy ignore list — documented, reviewed exceptions only.
#
# CVE-2026-14257 / GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg — brace-expansion DoS via unbounded
# expansion length.
#
# Why ignored (not explotable in this project):
#   - Reaches the tree ONLY through eslint (a devDependency) → its transitive
#     minimatch@3 → brace-expansion@1.1.16. eslint never ships to production
#     (the Dockerfile builds a standalone bundle without devDependencies).
#   - The attack is a DoS via a malicious brace glob passed to expand(); eslint
#     only ever expands OUR own config globs, never user input.
#   - No viable fix exists yet: the patched brace-expansion (>=5.0.8) is API-
#     incompatible with minimatch@3 (which eslint 9 core depends on), and
#     eslint 10 can't be adopted because eslint-plugin-react (pulled by
#     eslint-config-next / Next 16) does not support eslint 10 yet.
#
# Revisit when eslint-config-next ships plugins compatible with eslint 10, or
# when a patched brace-expansion lands in the 1.x line. Tracked in issue #27.
CVE-2026-14257
